vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "To normalize a vector $x,$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\frac{x}{‖x‖}.$ Therefore, to normalize $x,$ we first calculate $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+1+4+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $x$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{-1}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{-2}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-74147/selection/5ce177c99c66166d5e7801445de496e18fc4679535b27fc6b27c445a387b58fe" :answer/id #uuid "b24e16e3-76af-5be1-9e35-be16c50f7460" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74147/selection/0e6045045e8d44c6d532efcfcdbd628329722c6adac3affe6e09130171b99b7e" :answer/id #uuid "fda996af-f034-58cf-9e84-9168239fd44d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74147/selection/c344354bfadd2394613bcd0132254f37c6aa30c6dee63f9cbf3d8c5177d78f58" :answer/id #uuid "207e7f9f-285d-59d0-a8ed-6c5d19219205" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74147/selection/bb39b764b20b337e42a593c2738414e1598a4bc7000e5b77f30b875138e523ff" :answer/id #uuid "4d7ceb31-5bd3-5fe0-b12b-a7a5bfc9621f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74147/selection/23a36d37c157a6bd27c983051f683c62fb5563cae36db49f2133d2d6b8886b04" :answer/id #uuid "d1080d30-e708-5f1a-8556-d7750c6a76e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74147/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "08f557b4-83d0-5a22-a870-272fa05719ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74147/selection/23a36d37c157a6bd27c983051f683c62fb5563cae36db49f2133d2d6b8886b04" :answer-field/choices ["q-74147/selection/5ce177c99c66166d5e7801445de496e18fc4679535b27fc6b27c445a387b58fe" "q-74147/selection/0e6045045e8d44c6d532efcfcdbd628329722c6adac3affe6e09130171b99b7e" "q-74147/selection/c344354bfadd2394613bcd0132254f37c6aa30c6dee63f9cbf3d8c5177d78f58" "q-74147/selection/bb39b764b20b337e42a593c2738414e1598a4bc7000e5b77f30b875138e523ff" "q-74147/selection/23a36d37c157a6bd27c983051f683c62fb5563cae36db49f2133d2d6b8886b04"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74147" :question/id #uuid "1d8008bb-a2a5-505a-9588-d2adba2b74d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-74147" :question/problem "Normalize the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "To normalize a vector $x,$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\frac{x}{‖x‖}.$ Therefore, to normalize $x,$ we first calculate $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+0+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $x$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74147/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae41d849-9def-540c-8985-8fbeec679991"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74147"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39862/selection/4de22ed8a19ed1b508bdadba179c3d5a008d6e664f5a25941302c5fdf651d9c7" :answer/id #uuid "44a73934-239d-5ee4-a24a-c144e8aaa375" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\pm 7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39862/selection/9b31e64d23b595e0c195e0b305a1a1f8574b3a3f342febf59bccc4398489de8e" :answer/id #uuid "951c68a3-c15d-5dd8-bb39-c8257da85daa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\pm 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39862/selection/8a6408a0ab4c9671f793a9c44f23f8bb0249d37417a0f50ef6d390f7b0405dbc" :answer/id #uuid "a59afa8c-fa38-5477-8f44-3cdc0fb56bd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\pm \\sqrt{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39862/selection/3aba9574e0b3355915c8f0d77edec9fa3c1135d0179190a9ab29c90917997b1f" :answer/id #uuid "f4c5ae8e-300a-5d7c-aa32-93d7a7a146ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\pm \\sqrt{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39862/selection/930aa67973bd4fd4bf01af24835761decaafb47d60965d54669e8c85c384abe4" :answer/id #uuid "408952fd-d9fa-5269-9971-35af17a9735f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39862/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e33833f9-70cb-5f3b-aa4f-07f0c54fe178" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39862/selection/3aba9574e0b3355915c8f0d77edec9fa3c1135d0179190a9ab29c90917997b1f" :answer-field/choices ["q-39862/selection/4de22ed8a19ed1b508bdadba179c3d5a008d6e664f5a25941302c5fdf651d9c7" "q-39862/selection/9b31e64d23b595e0c195e0b305a1a1f8574b3a3f342febf59bccc4398489de8e" "q-39862/selection/8a6408a0ab4c9671f793a9c44f23f8bb0249d37417a0f50ef6d390f7b0405dbc" "q-39862/selection/3aba9574e0b3355915c8f0d77edec9fa3c1135d0179190a9ab29c90917997b1f" "q-39862/selection/930aa67973bd4fd4bf01af24835761decaafb47d60965d54669e8c85c384abe4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39862" :question/id #uuid "c4825ebc-e078-543f-a174-111e5aa6d9a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-39862" :question/problem "Find $k$, if $u=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9} \\\\ \\frac{k}{9} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{8}{9}\\end{aligned}]$ is a unit vector." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the norm of the vector $x$ in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{u}_{1}^{2}+{u}_{2}^{2}+{u}_{3}^{2}+{u}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{9})}^{2}+{(\\frac{k}{9})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+{(\\frac{8}{9})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{81}+\\frac{{k}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{64}{81}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{74+{k}^{2}}{81}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $‖u‖=1,$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{74+{k}^{2}}{81}} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{74+{k}^{2}} & =9 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{74+{k}^{2}})}^{2} & ={9}^{2} \\\\ 74+{k}^{2} & =81 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =7 \\\\ k & =\\pm \\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-39862/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae41d849-9def-540c-8985-8fbeec679991"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39862"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74151/selection/7757eb