stion/math-academy-id "q-74151" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -k \\\\ 2k \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Find $k$, if the distance between the vectors is $\\text{d}(x,y)=2\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the distance between $x$ and $y$ in terms of $k:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{y}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3-k)^{2}+(-k-(-1))^{2}+(2k-0)^{2}+(0-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9-6k+{k}^{2}+{k}^{2}-2k+1+4{k}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}-8k+14}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $\\text{d}(x,y)=2\\sqrt{3},$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}-8k+14} & =2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {(\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}-8k+14})}^{2} & ={(2\\sqrt{3})}^{2} \\\\ 6{k}^{2}-8k+14 & =12 \\\\ 6{k}^{2}-8k+2 & =0 \\\\ 3{k}^{2}-4k+1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the quadratic formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-4)\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}-4(3)(1)}}{2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{4}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 2}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 1}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives $k=1$ and $k=\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-74151/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae41d849-9def-540c-8985-8fbeec679991"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74151"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74138/selection/2b643065c856ed9a8091e4af092d723d7f31855d6f8993f942de6a86e92baf49" :answer/id #uuid "dc674f79-0009-5dca-9636-003a0d40e527" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74138/selection/f85dc445b13146